+# Stream protocol UDP / framing verification — 2026-10-30
+
+## Identity and scope
+
+Authored in a detached product worktree based on clean generated core
+`74f4c88b6e6243d858f45e172f18e4aa845d5f7f`, following separate chained-UDP
+fail-closed commit `2f89852` (already integrated independently). Original upstream
+`/workspace/shared/vp_core` is not edited. No Cargo manifest/lock change.
+
+The first source patch corrects VLESS partial-write/response buffering and VMess
+request padding, security=none wire format, four-byte response header, partial
+header reads, buffered write acceptance, canonical TCP chunk size, body nonce
+exhaustion and bounded auth-ID replay rejection. The second adds command-UDP and
+its tests. Final combined source, not the intermediate first patch alone, was
+compiled and executed in the author worktree.
+
+## Actual executed results
+
+Rust `--locked`, jobs=1, incremental=0, dev/test debug=0; shared
+`.local-cache/product-core-target`. No worker binary was rebuilt or overwritten.
+
+- 24 focused unit/composition tests PASS: VLESS4, VMess8, Trojan1, packet pool3,
+  existing server stream composition8 (TLS/WS/H2/Upgrade TCP regressions included).
+- 4 local integration tests PASS: all five modes' TCP100KB; IPv4/IPv6 UDP
+  1/128/4096/8192/15000/60000-byte payloads (plus empty datagrams except
+  VMess-none); multi-target identity and stable per-target source; canceled
+  receive recovery; explicit oversize/UDP-disabled/host-denied errors; captured
+  host authority; nonloopback/domain rejection before DNS/socket; scope cleanup.
+- 2 explicitly enabled independent integration matrix tests PASS against
+  unmodified official protocol libraries, **both directions**, VLESS/Trojan and
+  VMess AES-128-GCM/ChaCha20-Poly1305/none. TCP, IPv4/IPv6 UDP, wrong credentials,
+  stale VMess timestamp, VMess auth-ID replay, authenticated-body corruption,
+  global padding, multi-target/multi-size and generation cleanup are exercised.
+- Official library references: sing-vmess `a0c58542bd9d`, sing-box v1.14.4
+  `transport/trojan`, Go1.26.10. `go mod verify` PASS. Every compiled dependency
+  other than the root module is compared to v1.14.4's official go.sum; the root
+  module is independently checksum-database verified.
+- Rustfmt on changed Rust source/tests and `git diff --check` PASS.
+
+Durable raw logs and reference build/module/binary hashes are in the product
+`integration/stream-evidence/`, with final and earlier failed runs separately
+named. Initial fixture buffer ownership/headroom errors and a real VMess TCP
+chunk-size incompatibility were corrected; only final reruns are PASS.
+
+## Bounds and deliberate fail-closed boundaries
+
+- Clients send UDP only over their configured proxy transport; no direct UDP
+  fallback. VLESS/VMess fixed-destination commands use one proxy stream per
+  destination. At most16 sessions,16 queued frames per session/response queue,
+  10-second open/write deadline,120-second request-idle lifetime. Owned tracked
+  open/read/write tasks abort on drop and generation shutdown. Direct server
+  forwarding checks destination policy before DNS and uses protected constructors.
+- Maximum ordinary UDP payload65507. Independent VMess acceptance is bounded to
+  15000 bytes because this official library's UDP writer chunks larger payloads;
+  larger same-engine framing tests are not independent interoperability evidence.
+- `udp:false` errors. Chained UDP errors instead of bypassing its dialer. VMess
+  legacy alterId UDP, authenticated-length/connection-reuse options and unknown
+  wire flags error explicitly. VMess-none zero-length chunks are reserved for EOF
+  and empty writes are rejected rather than silently discarded.
+- No XUDP/packetaddr/mux or REALITY/Vision claim. VLESS Vision remains fail closed.
+  Existing carrier composition tests are TCP regressions; this is not an
+  independent all-carrier/TLS/Android packet-runtime acceptance matrix.
+- VLESS/Trojan have no standalone UDP replay authentication; their authenticated
+  encrypted carrier is a separate security layer. The raw protocol tests do not
+  manufacture replay-protection claims for these protocols.
+- No capability catalog/readiness flags were promoted. This work does not reduce
+  the full21-preset product release scope or certify any merged identity until
+  the integration owner replays/tests the promoted patchset.
