+# Independent stream protocol-library peer (test only)
+
+The adapter invokes unchanged `sing-vmess` commit
+`a0c58542bd9d99b00ea0c3cfacce6f03cf8a4017` and the `transport/trojan`
+package of official `sing-box v1.14.4`, commit
+`c005f35300ce76427dc285481ec5695f5b179cd2`.
+All compiled dependency identities are checked against that release's `go.sum`;
+the root sing-box module itself is Go-checksum-database verified. No protocol,
+KDF, cipher, authentication or wire framing is reimplemented by this Go adapter.
+It never constructs sing-box NetworkManager or invokes its CLI.
+
+Only `127.0.0.1`/`::1` listeners and explicitly checked loopback-IP forwarding
+are permitted. Credentials arrive over stdin and exist only for the test process.
+No host routes, firewall, TUN, system proxy, installation, persistent key, publishing
+or production engine substitution occurs. This Go module is never a Cargo
+production dependency or shipped runtime artifact.
+
+The VLESS adapter uses the library's `PacketConn.Read/Write` interface, converting
+only the caller's buffer ownership to sing's `network.PacketConn`. VMess disables
+only the library service's optional first-read packet-size heuristic so fragmented
+legitimate TCP writes can be tested; protocol validation/AEAD/replay remain intact.
+VLESS/Trojan UDP bodies are tested up to 60000 bytes; the pinned sing-vmess writer
+splits bodies above its 15000-byte chunk writer MTU, so independent VMess datagram
+acceptance is explicitly bounded to 15000 bytes (larger Rust-only framing tests are
+not presented as independent acceptance). Global-padding AEAD requests are tested.
+Authenticated-length, legacy alterId UDP, XUDP/packetaddr, mux and Vision UDP are
+explicit unsupported boundaries, not aliases of ordinary command-UDP.
+
+Authorized build and test (one job, conditional free-space guard):
+
+```
+GOMAXPROCS=1 GOFLAGS=-p=1 go mod verify
+GOMAXPROCS=1 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -p=1 -mod=readonly -trimpath -buildvcs=false -o reference-stream .
+VP_STREAM_REFERENCE=/absolute/path/reference-stream cargo test --locked -p vp-protocol --test stream_library_interop -- --ignored --nocapture --test-threads=1
+```
+
+This directory is source and dependency provenance. See the durable project
+`integration/stream-evidence` for actual build/test outcomes; the existence of this
+harness does not assert that an ignored test was executed or passed.
